### Any additional comments?

Assertion functions are useful to ensure we only run code in the expected environment,
for example: browser page, vs browser worker, vs Node.js. Or production vs development vs test.

```js
function assertDev() {
  // condition is removed by rollup -> the function always throws
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production") {
    throw new Error("This should not run in prod");
  }
}

function setup() {
  // can check for an environment variable or a global via `transform.define`
  if (process.env.TYPO === "developmen") {
    assertDev();
    // Set up dev tools here for example
    console.log("...");
  }
}

setup();
```
